<title>USA: CME to halve Mexican peso options strike intervals.</title>
<headline>CME to halve Mexican peso options strike intervals.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange said Thursday it would cut in half the strike price intervals for its options on Mexican peso futures, effective May 19.</p>
<p>The exchange, in a members' notice, said it would list the futures-options at strike price intervals of $0.00125 per New Mexican peso.</p>
<p>Currently, peso futures-options exercise prices are listed at $0.0025 intervals.</p>
<p>&quot;The finer strike interval will provide market participants increased trading opportunities and more precise hedging,&quot; the notice said. ((DerivativesDesk(312)408-8750)) E-mail:derivatives@reuters.com</p>
